   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening livelihood recovery of COVID-19 most affected rural communities in Cambodia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">promoting adoption of safe, nutritious and climate resilient agriculture with emphasis on short cycle agricultural production (vegetables, chicken, walking catfish, and frog), to ensure access to nutritious food and livelihood diversification; (ii) enabling vulnerable households? access to immediate cash needs and generate income through cash for work for community infrastructure rehabilitation/development and improving access to financial services from MFIs and ARDB through strengthening new and existing women saving and business groups; (iii) helping small farmers and rural communities to access domestic markets, and raising public awareness on the quality and safety of local products; and (iv) strengthening policy dialogue on food safety among key players to foster policy coherence, coordination and implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
